    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bambara-people">Bamana</a> kingdom on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, founded around 1712 by Biton Kulibali, who turned a young men’s association into an army.</li><li>Its power rested on the tonjon, soldiers of captive origin, and on the trade of Muslim Maraka towns such as Sinsani.</li><li>It resisted the Fulbe <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihads</a> until Umar Tall took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Ségou</a> in 1861; its kings live on in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griots">griots</a>’ epics.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mungo-park">Mungo Park</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Ségou</a> in 1796, King Monzon (Mansong) would not receive him but sent him 5,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cowrie-shell">cowries</a> to buy food for his journey.</p></aside>
    </section>

